# 25. Conclusion

The Academic Integrity & Similarity Case Management System provides a structured approach to managing academic integrity investigations.

It connects assignment submissions, similarity reports, flags, investigation cases, reviewers, evidence, decisions and appeals in one application.

The most important principle is that a similarity flag should initiate a fair investigation rather than automatically establish misconduct.

The system emphasizes proper validation, traceability, reviewer independence and transparent decision-making.

Through this project, practical knowledge is applied in full-stack development, REST API design, relational database architecture, backend business logic, data validation and automated testing.